# React Component Guide

## Page Component Pattern

Every page follows this structure:

```jsx
import { useEffect, useState } from 'react';
import { useLanguage } from '../contexts/LanguageContext';
import LoadingSpinner from '../components/ui/LoadingSpinner';

export default function PageName() {
  const [data, setData] = useState([]);
  const [loading, setLoading] = useState(true);
  const [error, setError] = useState(null);
  const { language, t } = useLanguage();

  useEffect(() => {
    fetchData()
      .then(setData)
      .catch(setError)
      .finally(() => setLoading(false));
  }, []);

  return (
    <div className="page-pagename">
      <section className="page-hero">
        <h1>{t('nav.pageName')}</h1>
        <p>Subtitle text</p>
      </section>
      <section className="section">
        <div className="container">
          {loading && <LoadingSpinner center size="lg" />}
          {error && <div className="error-state">...</div>}
          {!loading && !error && data.length === 0 && <p className="empty-state">...</p>}
          {!loading && !error && data.length > 0 && (/* render data */)}
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Layout Structure

- `Layout.jsx` wraps `Navbar` + `<main>` + `Footer`.
- Login and Register pages render **outside** Layout (no shared nav/footer).
- All other routes render inside Layout.

## Available Contexts

### `useAuth()` (from `AuthContext`)
Returns `{ user, profile, loading }`.
- `user` — Firebase Auth user object or null.
- `profile` — Firestore `users/{uid}` document or null.
- `loading` — true until initial auth state resolves.

### `useLanguage()` (from `LanguageContext`)
Returns `{ language, changeLanguage, t }`.
- `language` — `"en"` or `"am"`.
- `changeLanguage(lang)` — switch language, persists to localStorage.
- `t(key)` — resolve translation key with fallback.

## Reusable UI Components

### `EventCard` — `src/components/ui/EventCard.jsx`
Props: `{ event }` — renders event card with date badge, title, time, location, description, link.

Wrap lists in `.events-grid` (Home) or `.events-list` (Events page); both use the same CSS grid (`repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, 270px), 1fr))`) so up to four cards fit per row in the max-width container. Narrow card cells stack the date block above the info via an `@container` query on `.event-card`. Cards use column flex (`height: 100%`) so row heights match; the Learn more link uses `margin-top: auto` and `align-self: center` at the bottom of `.event-card-info`.

### `SermonCard` — `src/components/ui/SermonCard.jsx`
Props: `{ sermon }` — renders sermon card with thumbnail, category badge, title, speaker, date, actions.

### `LoadingSpinner` — `src/components/ui/LoadingSpinner.jsx`
Props: `{ size = 'md', center = false }` — sizes: `sm`, `md`, `lg`.

### `ProtectedRoute` — `src/components/ui/ProtectedRoute.jsx`
Props: `{ children, adminOnly = false }` — redirects to `/login` if not authenticated, to `/` if not admin (when `adminOnly`).

## Custom Hooks

### `useFirestoreCollection(collectionName, queryConstraints)`
Real-time listener on a Firestore collection. Returns `{ data, loading, error }`.

### `useFirestoreDoc(collectionName, docId)`
Real-time listener on a single Firestore document. Returns `{ data, loading, error }`.

## Form Pattern (react-hook-form)

```jsx
const { register, handleSubmit, reset, formState: { errors } } = useForm();

<form onSubmit={handleSubmit(onSubmit)} className="form">
  <div className="form-group">
    <label>Field Name *</label>
    <input {...register('fieldName', { required: 'Required' })} className="form-input" />
    {errors.fieldName && <span className="form-error">{errors.fieldName.message}</span>}
  </div>
  <button type="submit" className="btn btn-primary btn-full">Submit</button>
</form>
```

## Button Classes

| Class | Style |
|-------|-------|
| `.btn-primary` | On light: brand blue; on dark hero/CTA: accent red (`index.css` scoped) |
| `.btn-outline` | Transparent with primary blue border |
| `.btn-outline-light` | White border (for dark backgrounds) |
| `.btn-ghost` | Transparent, no border |
| `.btn-sm` | Small size |
| `.btn-lg` | Large size |
| `.btn-full` | Full width |
